{"ghsa_id":"GHSA-w4qr-p94g-mjhv","cve_id":null,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/security-advisories/GHSA-w4qr-p94g-mjhv","html_url":"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/security/advisories/GHSA-w4qr-p94g-mjhv","summary":"Wasmtime wasi:http implementation panics with a zero timeout supplied","description":"### Impact\r\n\r\nWasmtime's implementation of `wasi:http` for both WASIp2 and WASIp3 contained a bug where when a 0 timeout was specified for the between-bytes-timeout request option this would trigger a panic on the host. The duration from the guest was forwarded directly to a Tokio API, a dependency of Wasmtime's `wasi:http` implementation, which is documented as panicking when a 0 duration was pased to it. A guest-triggerable panic on the host is considered a denial-of-service vulnerability in Wasmtime.\r\n\r\nThis bug affects any user of the `wasmtime-wasi-http` crate in Wasmtime when the `default-send-request` Cargo feature is enabled, which is enabled by default. Embedders which do not use Wasmtime's implementation of `wasi:http` are unaffected.\r\n\r\n### Patches\r\n\r\nWasmtime 48.0.4 and 49.0.2 have been released which fix this panic by clamping the timeout duration to 1 nanosecond.\r\n\r\n### Workarounds\r\n\r\nThere is no known workaround for this issue at this time and it's recommended that users upgrade or change their embedding to not provide `wasi:http` APIs.\r\n\r\n","severity":"medium","author":null,"publisher":{"login":"alexcrichton","id":64996,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0OTk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64996?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton","html_url":"https://github.com/alexcrichton","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"identifiers":[{"value":"GHSA-w4qr-p94g-mjhv","type":"GHSA"}],"state":"published","created_at":null,"updated_at":"2026-10-02T19:39:16Z","published_at":"2026-10-02T19:39:15Z","closed_at":null,"withdrawn_at":null,"submission":null,"vulnerabilities":[{"package":{"ecosystem":"rust","name":"wasmtime-wasi-http"},"vulnerable_version_range":">= 46.0.0, < 48.0.4, >= 49.0.0, < 49.0.2","patched_versions":"48.0.4, 49.0.2","vulnerable_functions":[]}],"cvss_severities":{"cvss_v3":{"vector_string":null,"score":null},"cvss_v4":{"vector_string":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:L/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N","score":5.9}},"cwes":[],"cwe_ids":[],"credits":[{"login":"smaeljaish771","type":"reporter"},{"login":"KeenSecurityLab","type":"sponsor"}],"credits_detailed":[{"user":{"login":"smaeljaish771","id":266604088,"node_id":"U_kgDOD-QOOA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266604088?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smaeljaish771","html_url":"https://github.com/smaeljaish771","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smaeljaish771/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smaeljaish771/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smaeljaish771/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smaeljaish771/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smaeljaish771/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smaeljaish771/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smaeljaish771/repos",